    {
      "order": 9,
      "depth": 1,
      "type": "text",
      "content": "Sthala Puranam:\nThis kshethram again does not have a particular sthala puranam of its own. This kshethram is closely related to Tiruneeragam and Tirukaaragam. Kaarvaanam means a sky filled with clouds. The world cannot survive without water, and clouds play a crucial role in bringing water to the world. Thus, the Lord standing here is an embodiment of rain clouds bringing rain to the world, helping it survive.",
      "textFontSizeHint": 16
    }
